---
id: home
description: "KCD Your City 2099 is coming on 15 May! A day of Kubernetes and Cloud Native talks with the local community. Tickets are available now."
---
{{ layout "layouts/home.vto" }}

{{#
    The home page: the hero (layouts/home.vto puts the `hero` slot into a
    full-screen `hero.frame`), then the sections, each a `ui.band` written
    here over the theme's components. Collection sections (sponsors,
    keynotes, organizers) check their list length; the venue always renders. A section
    over a page (the sponsoring invitation, the agenda teaser) checks that
    the page is in the build, so a `draft: true` drops it. The copy is this
    edition's and lives here, next to the conditions that pick it. This is
    the site with the programme out: the agenda teaser joins the sections
    (the agenda page is in the build), tickets are available, the call for
    papers is closed; the CFP section below stays, gated on `cfp.open`, for
    the record. Copy that changes at a deadline is timed
    text (ui.text), so the page reads right between the deadline and the
    next deploy. Other shapes of home page are in the theme's
    showcase (showcase/src/home/).
#}}

{{# Regular tickets: early-bird pricing ended on 31 March 2099. "Available",
    not "on sale": with the discount over, "on sale" reads as one. The call for
    papers is closed (cfp.open in cfp.yaml). #}}
{{ slot hero }}
    {{ comp.hero.intro({
        badge: "Tickets available",
        tagline: "The Kubernetes Community Days are coming to Your City.",
        lede: "Tickets are available now, grab yours and join us.",
    }) }}

    {{ comp ui.actions }}
        {{ comp.ui.button({ label: "Get tickets", page: "tickets", icon: "fa-ticket", style: "primary" }) }}
        {{ comp.ui.button({ label: "I'm attending", page: "attending", icon: "fa-image", style: "secondary" }) }}
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /slot }}

{{# Call for papers, while `cfp.open`: a timed pill and lede, the first-timers box, the buttons. #}}
{{ if cfp.open }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "call-for-papers" } }}
        {{ comp.ui.heading({
            pill: { html: "Call for papers open", until: cfp.deadline, after: "Call for papers closed" },
            title: "Share your story on the KCD Your City stage",
            lede: {
                html: "Whether it's a hard-won production lesson, a deep dive into a cloud native project, or a fresh perspective on the ecosystem, we want to hear from you. Submit your talk and help shape KCD Your City 2099.",
                until: cfp.deadline,
                after: "The call for papers is now closed. Thank you to everyone who submitted a proposal and helped shape KCD Your City 2099.",
            },
        }) }}

        <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl rounded-lg border border-secondary bg-secondary/20 p-8 text-left">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: "fa-hand-holding-heart", classes: "mt-1 shrink-0 text-3xl text-accent" }) }}
                <div>
                    <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold text-black">First-time speakers are welcome</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700">
                        Never spoken at a conference before? This is the perfect place
                        to start. We're happy to help you write your first proposal,
                        shape your talk and prepare for the stage. Everyone starts
                        somewhere, so reach out and we'll support you every step of
                        the way.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {{ comp ui.actions }}
            {{ comp ui.until { time: cfp.deadline } }}
                {{ comp.ui.button({
                    label: "Submit your talk",
                    href: cfp.url,
                    icon: "fa-microphone-lines",
                    style: "primary",
                    external: true,
                }) }}
            {{ /comp }}
            {{ comp ui.after { time: cfp.deadline } }}
                {{ comp.ui.button({
                    label: "Submissions closed",
                    icon: "fa-microphone-lines",
                    style: "primary",
                    disabled: true,
                }) }}
            {{ /comp }}
            {{ comp.ui.button({ label: "CFP FAQ", page: "cfp-faq", icon: "fa-circle-question", style: "outlineAccent" }) }}
            {{ comp.ui.button({
                label: "Ask us for help",
                href: social.discord,
                icon: "fa-brands fa-discord",
                style: "outline",
                external: true,
            }) }}
        {{ /comp }}
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}

{{# "What is KCD Your City?": the two paragraphs the page opens its content with. #}}
{{ comp ui.band { id: "about" } }}
    {{ comp ui.heading { title: `What is ${event.name}?` } }}
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6 rich-text">
            <a href="https://www.cncf.io/kcds/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kubernetes Community Days</a>
            (or KCD) is a
            <a href="https://www.cncf.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF)</a>
            supported event that takes place in dozens of cities every year. KCD Your
            City is the first edition in our city: a day for the local cloud native
            community to learn from each other and from guests from further afield.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 rich-text">
            KCDs are community-organized events that gather adopters and
            technologists from open source and cloud native communities for
            education, collaboration, and networking.
        </p>
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /comp }}

{{# Sponsors: one `ui.logo` row per tier in sponsors.yaml, in file order; a tier's `style` sizes its row and items. Logos share a 500x300 canvas. #}}
{{ if sponsors.tiers.length }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "sponsors" } }}
        {{ comp.ui.heading({ title: "Our sponsors", lede: `Companies that make ${event.name} possible` }) }}
        <div class="space-y-12">
            {{ for tier of sponsors.tiers }}
                <div class="text-center">
                    <h3 class="mb-6 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500">
                        {{ tier.name }}
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="mx-auto flex flex-wrap justify-center {{ tier.style.container }}">
                        {{ for item of tier.logos }}
                            <li class="{{ tier.style.item }}">
                                {{ comp.ui.logo({ name: item.name, logo: item.logo, href: item.url, width: 500, height: 300 }) }}
                            </li>
                        {{ /for }}
                    </ul>
                </div>
            {{ /for }}
        </div>
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}
{{# Keynotes: a `comp.keynote` card per entry in keynotes.yaml. Prepare the announcement on a branch, merge on the day. #}}
{{ if keynotes.speakers.length }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "keynotes", tone: "secondary" } }}
        {{ comp.ui.heading({
            title: "Keynote speakers",
            lede: `The keynotes open and close the day: industry leaders with their
                take on what's changing for the people who keep software running.`,
        }) }}
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            {{ for speaker of keynotes.speakers }}
                {{ comp.keynote(speaker) }}
            {{ /for }}
        </div>
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}

{{# Agenda teaser: one random talk (session.teaser) under an intro that counts them; keynotes and cancelled talks left out; only while the agenda page is in the build. #}}
{{ set talks = search.page("id=agenda")
    ? schedule.sessions.filter((s) => s.format !== "Keynote" && !s.cancelled && s.speakers.length > 0)
    : [] }}
{{ if talks.length }}
    {{ set agendaLede }}
        {{ talks.length }} talks{{ if schedule.rooms.length > 1 }}
        across {{ schedule.rooms.length }} tracks{{ /if }} follow
        the keynotes. Here's a sneak peek.
    {{ /set }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "agenda" } }}
        {{ comp.ui.heading({ pill: "Agenda", title: "Plan your day", lede: agendaLede }) }}

        {{ comp.session.teaser({ talks }) }}

        <div class="mt-10 text-center">
            {{ comp.ui.button({
                label: "See the full agenda",
                page: "agenda",
                icon: "fa-calendar-days",
                style: "primary",
            }) }}
        </div>
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}

{{# "What to expect?": the lede and the cards. #}}
{{ set whatToExpectLede }}
    A day of Kubernetes and Cloud Native, full of talks, hallway conversations
    and fun, ending with a party! We are a locally-focused but English-speaking
    community of engineers, developers, professionals and students of all
    things Cloud Native, coming together to celebrate our love and passion for
    technology.
{{ /set }}

{{ comp ui.band { id: "what-to-expect" } }}
    {{ comp.ui.heading({ title: "What to expect?", lede: whatToExpectLede }) }}
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-5 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6 md:col-span-2">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/10">
                {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: "fa-microphone-lines", classes: "text-accent text-xl" }) }}
            </span>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
                Two tracks of technically competent talks, relevant to the larger
                community and coming from end-users rather than vendors. The aim is
                to ensure the highest possible quality of sessions for all types of
                attendees.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-5 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/10">
                {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: "fa-star", classes: "text-accent text-xl" }) }}
            </span>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
                Special and well-known guests from the Open Source, DevOps and Cloud
                Native communities.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-5 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/10">
                {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: "fa-building-columns", classes: "text-accent text-xl" }) }}
            </span>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
                A modern venue in the heart of Your City, with room for hundreds of
                attendees.
            </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
{{ /comp }}

{{# Venue: the picture (linking to the venue page while it is in the build) beside name, address, summary, highlights and a button, from venue.yaml. Its own left-aligned heading; `ui.heading` centres. #}}
{{ set venuePage = search.page("id=venue") }}
{{ set venueUrl = venuePage ? venuePage.url : null }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "venue" } }}
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-center">
            {{# The space inside the if is required: Vento's autoTrim would glue the attributes. #}}
            <{{ venueUrl ? "a" : "div" }}
                {{ if venueUrl }} href="{{ venueUrl }}"{{ /if }}
                class="block overflow-hidden rounded-2xl shadow-xl"
            >
                <img
                    src="{{ venue.image.src }}"
                    srcset="{{ venue.image.src }} {{ venue.image.width }}w, {{ venue.image.src2x }} {{ venue.image.width * 2 }}w"
                    sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw"
                    alt="{{ venue.image.alt }}"
                    width="{{ venue.image.width }}"
                    height="{{ venue.image.height }}"
                    loading="lazy"
                    class="aspect-[3/2] w-full object-cover transition duration-300 hover:scale-105"
                />
            </{{ venueUrl ? "a" : "div" }}>
            <div>
                <span class="inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-1 rounded-full mb-6">
                    Venue
                </span>
                <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3 text-primary">
                    {{ venue.name }}
                </h2>
                <p class="flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-700 mb-6">
                    {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: "fa-location-dot", classes: "text-accent" }) }}
                    {{ venue.address.street }}, {{ venue.address.city }}
                </p>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6">
                    {{ venue.summary }}
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-8">
                    {{ for highlight of venue.highlights }}
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                            {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: highlight.icon, classes: "text-accent mt-1" }) }}
                            {{ highlight.text }}
                        </li>
                    {{ /for }}
                </ul>
                {{ comp.ui.button({
                    label: "Getting there and parking",
                    page: "venue",
                    icon: "fa-map-location-dot",
                    style: "primary",
                }) }}
            </div>
        </div>
    {{ /comp }}
{{# Sponsoring: the invitation, while the sponsors page is in the build (publishing it brings the band; the logos above show who already said yes). #}}
{{ if search.page("id=sponsors") }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "sponsoring", padding: "md" } }}
        {{ comp ui.heading {
            pill: "Sponsoring",
            title: `Partner with ${event.name}`,
            lede: `${event.name} is a community-organized, not-for-profit event, and it would not happen without its partners. Put your brand in front of the people who build and run cloud native infrastructure in this region.`,
        } }}
            {{ comp ui.actions }}
                {{ comp.ui.button({ label: "See the packages", page: "sponsors", icon: "fa-handshake", style: "primary" }) }}
            {{ /comp }}
        {{ /comp }}
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}

{{ comp ui.band { id: "video", padding: "md" } }}
    {{ comp.ui.heading({
        title: "A taste of what's coming",
        lede: "New to community days? This is what a KCD looks like: a day of talks, hallway conversations and people who care about the same things you do.",
    }) }}
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
            <div class="aspect-video">
                {{# A placeholder video id; replace it with yours. #}}
                <iframe
                    width="100%"
                    height="100%"
                    src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/AAAAAAAAAAA"
                    title="What is a Kubernetes Community Day?"
                    frameborder="0"
                    allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                    allowfullscreen
                    class="rounded-t-lg"
                ></iframe>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 text-center">
            {{ comp.ui.button({
                label: "Watch on YouTube",
                href: "#",
                icon: "fa-clock-rotate-left",
                style: "outline",
            }) }}
        </div>
    </div>
{{ /comp }}

{{# Media partners: 600x200 wordmarks, narrower than the sponsor logos so they do not look larger. #}}
{{ comp ui.band { id: "media-partners", padding: "md" } }}
    {{ comp.ui.heading({
        title: "Media partners",
        lede: "Thank you to our media partners. They help us tell the community about KCD Your City 2099.",
    }) }}
    <ul class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-8 gap-y-6 sm:gap-x-12">
        <li class="w-32 sm:w-40">
            {{ comp.ui.logo({ name: "Demo Weekly", logo: "/assets/media-partners/demo-weekly.svg", href: "#", width: 600, height: 200 }) }}
        </li>
    </ul>
{{ /comp }}

{{# Catch up: three ui.card links; the YouTube one keeps the brand red. #}}
{{ comp ui.band { id: "catch-up", padding: "md" } }}
    {{ comp.ui.heading({ title: "Catch up with the community" }) }}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        {{ comp.ui.card({
            icon: "fa-people-group",
            title: "The meetup",
            text: "KCD Your City grew out of the monthly cloud native meetup. Join the next one.",
            align: "center",
            href: "#",
            external: true,
        }) }}
        {{ comp.ui.card({
            icon: "fa-brands fa-youtube",
            iconClasses: "text-red-600",
            title: "Meetup recordings",
            text: "Watch the talks from previous meetups on YouTube.",
            align: "center",
            href: "#",
            external: true,
        }) }}
        {{ comp.ui.card({
            icon: "fa-newspaper",
            iconClasses: "text-primary",
            title: "Newsletter",
            text: "A short monthly email about the community and the conference.",
            align: "center",
            href: "#",
            external: true,
        }) }}
    </div>
{{ /comp }}

{{# Organizers: a `comp.organizer` card per entry in organizers.yaml, in a centred flex-wrap row (wider than the other sections: the cards are horizontal). #}}
{{ if organizers.people.length }}
    {{ comp ui.band { id: "organizers" } }}
        {{ comp.ui.heading({
            pill: "The team",
            title: "Meet the organizers",
            lede: `${event.name} is put together by volunteers from the local cloud
                native community, in their own free time.`,
        }) }}
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
            {{ for person of organizers.people }}
                {{ comp.organizer(person) }}
            {{ /for }}
        </ul>
    {{ /comp }}
{{ /if }}

{{# "Stay tuned": the dark band with the social links as stacked icons over `social`. #}}
{{ comp ui.band { id: "stay-tuned", tone: "primary", align: "center" } }}
    {{ comp.ui.heading({
        title: `Stay tuned for ${event.name} ${event.year}`,
        lede: "Follow us to be the first to hear about the call for papers, speakers, tickets and sponsorship opportunities.",
        inverse: true,
    }) }}
    {{ async function socialLink({ link, label, icon }) }}
        <a
            href="{{ link }}"
            {{ link |> newTab }}
            class="text-white hover:text-secondary transition-colors duration-300 flex flex-col items-center"
        >
            {{ comp.ui.icon({ name: icon, classes: "text-4xl mb-2" }) }}
            <span class="text-sm">{{ label }}</span>
        </a>
    {{ /function }}

    <div class="flex justify-center space-x-8">
        {{ comp.ui.socialLinks({ links: social, render: socialLink }) }}
    </div>
{{ /comp }}
